A final invariant audit caught a real bug before handoff: the radius-two filter rejected 4-cycles but did not explicitly reject triangles, so the “girth at least five” promise was too strong. I’m correcting the predicate and rerunning every local gate. This changes seeded instances, so the completed oracle transcripts no longer constitute exact replay evidence; the OpenRouter key is currently exhausted, and I’ll report that limitation plainly rather than conceal it.
